// VNEW_key_removed.schema — NEW: slots [Tier]int32, Tier {Bronze, Gold}, key Silver removed
//
// One of the fixed form's UNLAWFUL lineage rows (docs/FIXED-FORM-VERSIONING-TESTS.md,
// internal/fixedunlawful). The OLD and the NEW file of this pair differ by
// EXACTLY [Tier]int32, Tier {Bronze, Silver, Gold} -> {Bronze, Gold}. `lead` and `trail` bracket the row's field.
//
// THIS PAIR IS DELIBERATELY UNLAWFUL: SPEC §5.1 refuses a removed key ("variant removed", the keyed array follows
// its enum). A leg that lands each reader slot from the writer slot of the same
// key LOADS it.
// So this NEW side is generated and never dumped. The NEW reader must refuse old_key_removed.bin
// `layout_malformed` and write nothing (docs/FIXED-FORM-ALGORITHM.md §5.2, §5.4,
// §5.9 #30). Do not "fix" it.

package vnew_key_removed

enum Tier { Bronze, Gold }

fixed table KeyRemoved
{
    lead  uint32 = 1
    slots [Tier]int32
    trail uint32 = 2
}
